        Agent: a car placed stochastically at the bottom of a sinusoidal valley, with the only possible actions being the accelerations that can be applied to the car in either direction.
        
        Goal: strategically accelerate the car to reach the goal state on top of the right hill as quickly as possible once the agent is penalised with a reward of -1 for each timestep.

        Observation state: A 2D vector in the following order:

        Car position (meters): -Infinite to Infinite;
        Car velocity (meters per second): -Infinite to Infinite;
        
        Action are three discrete values:
        0 = Accelerate to the left 
        1 = Do not accelerate
        2 = Accelerate to the right
        
        Episode terminates when: 
           - the agent achieve the goal reaching the top of the hill (Car Position >= 0.5)
           - the lenght of the episode is 200 steps
        
            
